WEBVTT

00:01:31.100 --> 00:01:34.660
Scanning of Ryoko Kaminagi's
meta-body data is now complete.

00:01:35.100 --> 00:01:38.170
The lost and damaged
areas of her meta-body...

00:01:38.170 --> 00:01:40.900
have been almost perfectly restored.

00:01:42.140 --> 00:01:43.810
That's impossible!

00:01:43.810 --> 00:01:47.570
There's no way to reconstruct
data once it's been lost!

00:01:48.250 --> 00:01:50.580
It appears to have been integrated,
not reconstructed.

00:01:50.580 --> 00:01:55.380
I believe Sin gave some of
herself to Ryoko Kaminagi.

00:01:57.220 --> 00:02:00.210
Well then...
Does this present a threat to us?

00:02:00.590 --> 00:02:03.790
There are no traces of any
security-threat programs buried in her.

00:02:04.030 --> 00:02:06.460
So, you mean Kaminagi's back to normal?

00:02:06.800 --> 00:02:09.530
No, the areas that
form her emotions...

00:02:09.530 --> 00:02:13.330
are still trapped in the
Altair's meta-body buffer.

00:02:13.870 --> 00:02:17.770
They can only be reintegrated with her
during entanglement with the Altair.

00:02:18.610 --> 00:02:19.980
I see.

00:02:19.980 --> 00:02:24.310
So, all she really did was fill
in the damaged data sections.

00:02:24.780 --> 00:02:27.840
All right, continue work on
the repairs to the Oceanus.

00:02:28.650 --> 00:02:31.290
Take special care to make sure we're
not carrying any foreign objects.

00:02:31.290 --> 00:02:32.310
Aye, sir.

00:02:32.790 --> 00:02:36.190
Still, I wonder why Sin cured Ryoko.

00:02:36.660 --> 00:02:40.890
I would guess that it was an
act of good will on her part.

00:02:41.330 --> 00:02:43.800
Good will?
From a Reconstructant?

00:02:44.100 --> 00:02:48.470
Those things aren't human.
I can't believe they'd feel something like that.

00:02:51.310 --> 00:02:52.710
Kaminagi...

00:02:56.780 --> 00:02:59.010
Now then, I'd like to introduce a new transfer student.

00:02:59.080 --> 00:03:01.520
She'll be studying with you
in this class, starting today.

00:03:01.520 --> 00:03:03.620
Miss Shizuno Misaki.

00:03:03.620 --> 00:03:04.520
How do you do?

00:03:07.090 --> 00:03:08.850
I hope you'll all become friends with her.

00:03:20.640 --> 00:03:22.870
You like movies, don't you?

00:03:24.040 --> 00:03:28.270
That's a screenplay collection, isn't it?
You're always reading it!

00:03:29.680 --> 00:03:32.210
My name's Mizuki. Mizuki Tachibana.

00:03:32.720 --> 00:03:34.480
What sort of movies do you like?

00:03:35.550 --> 00:03:38.280
I really like "Last Year at Marienbad"
and stuff like that.

00:03:38.790 --> 00:03:39.950
Mizuki!

00:03:40.790 --> 00:03:42.390
The match is about to start!

00:03:42.390 --> 00:03:45.400
All right! I'm coming! I'll be right there!

00:03:45.400 --> 00:03:47.600
The tennis club asked me to help out.

00:03:47.600 --> 00:03:49.370
See you, Kaminagi!

00:03:49.370 --> 00:03:50.960
Come on! Come on!

00:03:53.300 --> 00:03:54.330
Kaminagi.

00:03:55.610 --> 00:03:56.500
Let's go.

00:04:00.210 --> 00:04:01.710
Um...

00:04:01.710 --> 00:04:03.750
Well, anyway...

00:04:03.750 --> 00:04:06.550
Isn't it great, Kaminagi?
You've recovered!

00:04:08.850 --> 00:04:12.410
I have to thank Sin for that,
even if she is the enemy.

00:04:14.230 --> 00:04:17.960
I know! Kaminagi, you wanna
go someplace and have fun?

00:04:17.960 --> 00:04:20.060
I know the Maihama server's kinda small,

00:04:20.060 --> 00:04:22.730
but there must be some places
we haven't visited yet!

00:04:23.170 --> 00:04:24.970
Let's celebrate together!

00:04:24.970 --> 00:04:26.990
Don't force yourself.

00:04:28.110 --> 00:04:31.540
I can't feel anything
the way I am now.

00:04:31.910 --> 00:04:33.440
Kaminagi...

00:04:33.440 --> 00:04:36.380
I have my memories
and can act as I want.

00:04:36.380 --> 00:04:39.410
I can live my life by
behaving logically, but...

00:04:39.780 --> 00:04:43.220
But I don't feel anything as I am now.

00:04:43.720 --> 00:04:45.660
Please don't act like I can.

00:04:45.660 --> 00:04:47.060
Kaminagi...

00:04:49.060 --> 00:04:51.400
I'm not forcing myself to do anything!

00:04:51.400 --> 00:04:54.330
I want to go out and have fun with you!

00:04:54.330 --> 00:04:56.630
Come out with me, Kaminagi!

00:04:57.540 --> 00:05:00.270
Where do you want to go?
What do you want to eat?

00:05:00.600 --> 00:05:02.440
It doesn't matter.

00:05:02.570 --> 00:05:05.570
Come on, anything.
Don't you want to do something?

00:05:07.910 --> 00:05:09.470
Kaminagi!

00:05:16.790 --> 00:05:18.360
Big news!

00:05:18.360 --> 00:05:19.190
What's up?

00:05:19.190 --> 00:05:21.490
There's a big sale in the market in town!

00:05:21.490 --> 00:05:23.960
Maybe they'll let me exchange this!

00:05:25.500 --> 00:05:26.990
They have nothing left!

00:05:43.550 --> 00:05:45.580
I'm going to bed.

00:05:45.580 --> 00:05:48.550
Sure. Good night.
And brush your teeth!

00:05:53.190 --> 00:05:55.060
Is it over?

00:06:02.530 --> 00:06:05.370
Are you enjoying the movies?

00:06:07.070 --> 00:06:08.970
I don't know.

00:06:09.070 --> 00:06:11.840
But I think I enjoy them.

00:06:12.710 --> 00:06:14.140
I see.

00:06:14.140 --> 00:06:15.810
You don't have to force yourself.

00:06:15.810 --> 00:06:17.880
I'm not forcing myself!

00:06:17.880 --> 00:06:20.710
I decided to watch movies
with you today, Kaminagi!

00:06:21.190 --> 00:06:22.950
He's coming after me!

00:06:22.950 --> 00:06:24.850
I've gotta get out of here, now!

00:06:27.290 --> 00:06:29.190
<i>What was she?</i>

00:06:29.360 --> 00:06:30.330
NO!!!

00:06:31.100 --> 00:06:34.090
<i>She risked such danger</i>
<i>infiltrating the Oceanus,</i>

00:06:35.700 --> 00:06:37.960
<i>and then just wandered around</i>
<i>asking weird questions.</i>

00:06:38.100 --> 00:06:41.830
And why do you fight?
Why, when you have no future?

00:06:42.540 --> 00:06:45.530
She wanted to know. Really, she did.

00:06:46.740 --> 00:06:48.710
The reason why we fight.

00:06:48.710 --> 00:06:50.580
You talked to her?!

00:06:50.580 --> 00:06:54.420
I told her there was something
irreplaceable I didn't want to lose.

00:06:55.420 --> 00:07:00.250
That I wanted to protect it. When I said that,
she said she finally understood.

00:07:03.790 --> 00:07:05.660
Kyo?

00:07:06.130 --> 00:07:10.260
How's the swim club?
Is the swim club all right?

00:07:11.240 --> 00:07:13.500
Shizuno-sempai transferred in today.

00:07:17.340 --> 00:07:18.330
Yeah.

00:07:18.440 --> 00:07:20.910
It wasn't a dream.

00:07:20.910 --> 00:07:25.120
I was led by Shizuno Misaki,
rode in that shining robot...

00:07:25.120 --> 00:07:27.850
And then... That passionate kiss from her...

00:07:43.770 --> 00:07:47.600
Um, boy, this movie's really lame!
Let's watch another one!

00:07:47.770 --> 00:07:50.040
Oh! This one's good, don't you think?

00:07:50.040 --> 00:07:53.410
C'mon, let's put this one in!
It looks great!

00:07:54.410 --> 00:07:57.350
Oh, this one's about Robin Hood, huh?

00:07:57.350 --> 00:08:00.750
I know this one!
He shoots an apple, right?

00:08:01.090 --> 00:08:04.920
Okay, let's get this started!
Hey, Kaminagi! Want some chips?

00:08:04.920 --> 00:08:07.390
Kyo, just now...

00:08:07.730 --> 00:08:11.030
Um, that was nothing.
Nothing at all...

00:08:11.030 --> 00:08:13.300
Never mind! Just forget it!

00:08:13.300 --> 00:08:15.530
Kyo, you're wrong.

00:08:16.570 --> 00:08:19.230
William Tell shot the apple.

00:08:22.870 --> 00:08:24.840
Commander? Commander!

00:08:26.280 --> 00:08:29.470
I'm sorry. It looked like you
were having a nightmare.

00:08:31.720 --> 00:08:32.550
Here.

00:08:33.750 --> 00:08:37.480
I guess even commanders have
bad dreams now and then.

00:08:39.160 --> 00:08:41.290
It's a layered structure, isn't it?

00:08:41.290 --> 00:08:45.090
We're ghosts who have
the ghosts of dreams.

00:08:45.760 --> 00:08:49.820
Perhaps... The people in our
dreams have dreams of their own.

00:08:51.840 --> 00:08:55.840
Then maybe we're dreams
that someone else is having.

00:08:55.840 --> 00:08:57.810
That may be true.

00:08:58.640 --> 00:09:00.910
Perhaps you can say
the only meaning we have...

00:09:00.910 --> 00:09:02.970
is as the dreams
of the quantum servers.

00:09:03.410 --> 00:09:05.640
Minato, wait outside, would you?

00:09:06.220 --> 00:09:07.880
Yes, sir.

00:09:11.020 --> 00:09:12.560
Well?

00:09:12.560 --> 00:09:16.220
We can't stop the march of time.
Things are moving even faster than we thought.

00:09:17.260 --> 00:09:18.430
I see.

00:09:18.430 --> 00:09:21.560
I wanted our position
to be more secure, but...

00:09:22.070 --> 00:09:23.830
Do we have a chance of winning?

00:09:23.830 --> 00:09:26.770
That depends on you and Kyo.
What about him?

00:09:26.770 --> 00:09:30.710
He has the combat skills.
The rest is a question of psychology.

00:09:31.110 --> 00:09:35.070
I don't care about his private life,
so long as he fights.

00:09:42.290 --> 00:09:44.720
<i>Oceanus, this is Altair.</i>

00:09:44.720 --> 00:09:48.090
<i>No enemies spotted in Romeo sector.</i>
<i>Patrol duty, complete.</i>

00:09:48.090 --> 00:09:49.890
<i>Request clearance for return transmission.</i>

00:09:50.390 --> 00:09:53.890
Oceanus, acknowledged.
You are clear for return transmission.

00:09:56.130 --> 00:09:58.000
Transmission preparations, complete.

00:09:58.000 --> 00:10:00.440
Q.L., two minutes to return limit.

00:10:01.540 --> 00:10:03.400
It's over?

00:10:04.110 --> 00:10:05.340
Short.

00:10:05.340 --> 00:10:07.400
Yeah, it was.

00:10:09.210 --> 00:10:11.550
Because you're a bird.

00:10:12.250 --> 00:10:16.020
As long as you have strength in
your wings, you should fly free.

00:10:16.450 --> 00:10:20.520
But once in a while, if you can,
come back to the tree.

00:10:20.520 --> 00:10:22.960
Because I'll always
be here waiting for you.

00:10:23.630 --> 00:10:24.920
Kaminagi...

00:10:25.160 --> 00:10:27.060
Silly!

00:10:27.060 --> 00:10:30.430
Did you already forget that line
from the movie we watched?

00:10:31.030 --> 00:10:33.670
Wha?! Of course I don't remember!

00:10:33.670 --> 00:10:35.730
We watched, like,
a million of them in one sitting!

00:10:36.770 --> 00:10:38.140
Hey, Kyo.

00:10:38.140 --> 00:10:39.370
What?

00:10:39.680 --> 00:10:41.880
Why'd you stop before?

00:10:41.880 --> 00:10:43.080
Stop what?

00:10:43.080 --> 00:10:44.170
Your kiss.

00:10:44.880 --> 00:10:47.780
Wha?! Don't be crazy!
I wasn't trying to!

00:10:48.090 --> 00:10:49.650
I wouldn't have minded.

00:10:49.650 --> 00:10:51.960
You're nuts!
That's totally not what it was!

00:10:51.960 --> 00:10:54.290
Wow, you're not usually such a gentleman.

00:10:54.660 --> 00:10:55.680
Shut up!

00:10:57.590 --> 00:11:01.050
Thank you, Kyo. For being with me.

00:11:01.570 --> 00:11:03.000
Kaminagi...

00:11:03.570 --> 00:11:05.270
One minute to return level!

00:11:05.270 --> 00:11:06.600
Initiate transmission.

00:11:08.370 --> 00:11:10.070
Kyo?

00:11:14.010 --> 00:11:16.140
See you later.

00:11:17.080 --> 00:11:18.340
Go! Go! Maihama!

00:11:18.480 --> 00:11:20.210
Go! Go!

00:11:26.390 --> 00:11:28.690
Agh! Ryoko! Help me!

00:11:30.890 --> 00:11:31.830
Um...

00:11:33.400 --> 00:11:34.600
Is she there?!

00:11:34.600 --> 00:11:35.100
No!

00:11:35.100 --> 00:11:37.530
Oh... Where'd Mizuki go?!

00:11:37.530 --> 00:11:38.660
Let's check down there!

00:11:38.740 --> 00:11:39.530
Right!

00:11:41.200 --> 00:11:43.240
Whew! Sorry about that.

00:11:43.240 --> 00:11:45.540
I like hanging out
with them for practice,

00:11:45.540 --> 00:11:47.870
but they want me for
out-of-school matches, too!

00:11:48.310 --> 00:11:51.040
Like I've got time for that
with the drama club!

00:11:51.380 --> 00:11:53.410
Oh! You've started
writing a screenplay?

00:11:53.780 --> 00:11:54.910
Mm.

00:11:55.150 --> 00:11:57.350
So, which is the real one?

00:11:57.820 --> 00:11:59.310
The title.

00:11:59.460 --> 00:12:03.480
I still haven't decided. I may end
up with a totally different title.

00:12:05.860 --> 00:12:06.600
There she is!

00:12:06.600 --> 00:12:07.530
Mizuki!

00:12:07.630 --> 00:12:10.400
- Agh! Yikes! Come on, guys!
- Gimme a break!

00:12:10.400 --> 00:12:13.500
- Come on! Just this once!
- Come on, I just can't do it, okay?

00:12:20.810 --> 00:12:23.540
A manufactured world, huh?

00:12:24.380 --> 00:12:25.750
Sogoru!

00:12:27.080 --> 00:12:29.450
Here you are!
I've been looking for you!

00:12:30.120 --> 00:12:32.620
Why haven't you been in school?

00:12:32.620 --> 00:12:37.180
Mr. Kurashige said he hasn't heard
anything from you and was worried.

00:12:38.160 --> 00:12:41.260
You haven't been doing any club
activities, either. Are you sick?

00:12:41.260 --> 00:12:42.770
Are you, Sogoru?

00:12:42.770 --> 00:12:43.960
Lay off!

00:12:46.640 --> 00:12:48.010
Just lay off.

00:12:48.010 --> 00:12:49.640
Sogoru...

00:12:49.640 --> 00:12:50.540
Tomigai!

00:12:50.540 --> 00:12:51.470
Yes?

00:12:51.540 --> 00:12:52.780
Yakisoba rolls!

00:12:52.780 --> 00:12:54.140
Coming up!

00:13:10.690 --> 00:13:13.030
What? You're still alive?

00:13:13.030 --> 00:13:15.020
What's the idea, ditching school?

00:13:15.900 --> 00:13:18.090
Stopped trying to get more
members for the swim club?

00:13:18.300 --> 00:13:20.470
Didn't take you long to give up, huh?

00:13:20.470 --> 00:13:23.740
Well, I figured you
weren't up to it, anyway.

00:13:23.740 --> 00:13:28.440
It's only right for the club to fail
with a coward like you running it.

00:13:32.820 --> 00:13:35.650
Hey! What's the idea, ignoring us?!

00:13:35.650 --> 00:13:36.950
Nothing.

00:13:36.950 --> 00:13:40.080
You dissin' me?! Why, you!

00:13:40.820 --> 00:13:44.160
Don't run from me!
What kind of chickenshit are you?!

00:13:46.100 --> 00:13:50.360
Today... Okita from the ping-pong club got
a sprain doing the broad jump in phys-ed.

00:13:51.800 --> 00:13:54.570
The tropical fish Kurage
was keeping all died,

00:13:54.570 --> 00:13:56.840
and he was depressed about it all day.

00:13:56.840 --> 00:13:59.040
And tomorrow,
Omizu is going to bring in...

00:13:59.040 --> 00:14:02.500
some neon tetras she's keeping at
her home and let him have some.

00:14:03.180 --> 00:14:07.410
It's an illusion...
Our lives! It's all fake!

00:14:07.750 --> 00:14:09.250
It's what?!

00:14:09.250 --> 00:14:11.590
Quit throwing this bullshit at us!

00:14:11.590 --> 00:14:13.780
All of us are just!

00:14:19.700 --> 00:14:22.160
Just what?! You got
something to say, then say it!

00:14:24.370 --> 00:14:27.140
Don't get so pretentious if you aren't serious!

00:14:27.140 --> 00:14:28.540
I'm always serious!

00:14:30.740 --> 00:14:32.870
Are you giving up on the swim club?!

00:14:33.010 --> 00:14:34.980
You're a god damned loser!

00:14:34.980 --> 00:14:37.280
You son of a bitch!

00:14:42.350 --> 00:14:46.760
Kyo, you shouldn't fight with them.
They're your friends.

00:14:47.190 --> 00:14:48.430
Who cares?

00:14:48.430 --> 00:14:52.360
In five months, they'll just
forget everything again.

00:14:52.360 --> 00:14:54.760
Even so, you shouldn't.

00:14:54.760 --> 00:14:55.870
Why not?

00:14:55.870 --> 00:15:00.430
Because it's better to be happy than to
keep doing the same stuff over and over.

00:15:01.570 --> 00:15:03.210
Right?

00:15:03.210 --> 00:15:03.900
Sure.

00:15:06.910 --> 00:15:08.780
Oh! Look at that!

00:15:08.880 --> 00:15:10.400
Kyo, take us down.

00:15:19.790 --> 00:15:22.890
Wow! It's so pretty!

00:15:22.890 --> 00:15:24.790
Kyo, let's go out!

00:15:28.300 --> 00:15:30.000
Sit-rep.

00:15:30.000 --> 00:15:34.060
The ship is currently moving south
off of the western Australian coast.

00:15:34.800 --> 00:15:36.930
The Altair is following us while on patrol.

00:15:37.540 --> 00:15:40.540
There's no indication of
Gards-orm forces approaching us.

00:15:40.540 --> 00:15:43.880
Once the Altair is back,
set course for Japan.

00:15:45.480 --> 00:15:46.820
Japan?

00:15:46.820 --> 00:15:49.310
The Oceanus is headed
for the Maihama server.

00:15:49.920 --> 00:15:51.250
Commander Shima!

00:15:51.250 --> 00:15:52.290
Yes?

00:15:52.290 --> 00:15:56.260
I'd like to ask why we're
returning to the Maihama server.

00:15:56.260 --> 00:15:57.830
You have some doubts?

00:15:57.830 --> 00:15:59.630
Whenever the ship gets near it,

00:15:59.630 --> 00:16:02.930
we increase the chances of
the enemy finding the server.

00:16:02.930 --> 00:16:06.730
Shouldn't we avoid approaching it
unless absolutely necessary?

00:16:07.140 --> 00:16:10.440
Moreover, this ship was recently
infiltrated by the enemy.

00:16:10.440 --> 00:16:13.430
Don't you think we should
avoid any careless risks?

00:16:16.150 --> 00:16:17.480
It's for maintenance.

00:16:19.650 --> 00:16:22.520
More accurately, to inspect the
quantum transmission system.

00:16:23.090 --> 00:16:24.350
Fosetta.

00:16:24.350 --> 00:16:25.260
Yes.

00:16:25.260 --> 00:16:31.190
The error rate has been slightly increasing
lately on access from the Maihama server.

00:16:31.430 --> 00:16:34.130
While it's still within
correction tolerances,

00:16:34.130 --> 00:16:38.470
I now believe it would be best
to adjust it as soon as possible.

00:16:38.470 --> 00:16:41.600
There you have it.
Do you agree with my decision?

00:16:44.510 --> 00:16:46.170
Something wrong?

00:16:46.840 --> 00:16:49.070
No. It's nothing.

00:16:54.380 --> 00:16:57.350
So pretty!
Kyo, have you heard this one?

00:16:57.990 --> 00:17:01.290
Long ago,
when two lovers were split up,

00:17:01.290 --> 00:17:05.520
the woman was so sad that her body
was transformed and became the lily.

00:17:06.030 --> 00:17:08.620
Yeah. That's a legend from
the Caucasus region, right?

00:17:09.070 --> 00:17:11.870
Wow. I wouldn't expect you to know that.

00:17:11.870 --> 00:17:13.860
Especially when you don't
even know about Robin Hood!

00:17:14.940 --> 00:17:17.170
There's more to that legend.

00:17:17.640 --> 00:17:21.950
In order to ensure that the girl who'd
become the lily would always have water,

00:17:21.950 --> 00:17:24.240
God transformed
the man into a rain cloud.

00:17:25.580 --> 00:17:29.210
In order to be together,
they both gave up being human.

00:17:29.750 --> 00:17:33.660
Kaminagi...
Are we no longer human?

00:17:35.290 --> 00:17:39.130
Between us Cerebrants,
looking at this real scenery...

00:17:39.130 --> 00:17:42.830
and the guys living in the artificial
world of the Maihama server,

00:17:42.830 --> 00:17:44.470
which of us are real?

00:17:44.470 --> 00:17:45.730
Kyo...

00:17:46.770 --> 00:17:49.170
I... don't hurt anymore.

00:17:50.740 --> 00:17:54.280
When Kawaguchi punched me,
I really wanted to hit back,

00:17:54.280 --> 00:17:56.750
but somewhere inside me,
I just lost the urge.

00:17:56.980 --> 00:18:00.540
I got angry because, no matter how much
he hit me, I don't think it really hurt me.

00:18:01.620 --> 00:18:04.890
I thought I was able to take it
because everything is fake, but...

00:18:04.890 --> 00:18:07.320
No. I'm not "taking it."

00:18:07.490 --> 00:18:09.520
I can't feel anything anymore!

00:18:11.360 --> 00:18:14.300
Even if I manage to make up
with them in five months,

00:18:14.300 --> 00:18:17.060
when the reset comes,
I'll have to start all over again!

00:18:17.700 --> 00:18:20.500
Then we'll make up again,
then we'll go back again...

00:18:20.500 --> 00:18:22.600
It's just impossible!

00:18:23.010 --> 00:18:25.410
But even though it's impossible,
they're serious about it!

00:18:26.380 --> 00:18:29.500
Even in that fake world,
they live their lives with meaning!

00:18:30.050 --> 00:18:34.180
I'm starting to wonder
if they're more real than me!

00:18:41.590 --> 00:18:43.180
You're wrong, Kyo.

00:18:44.560 --> 00:18:46.960
We're all fake.

00:18:47.760 --> 00:18:51.670
"Real" is someone who
can touch these flowers.

00:18:51.670 --> 00:18:53.670
Real is...

00:18:53.670 --> 00:18:56.760
The people who can
live in this real world!

00:18:57.540 --> 00:19:00.770
To live... in the real world, huh?

00:19:01.180 --> 00:19:03.650
Like that girl Sin that I met before.

00:19:07.080 --> 00:19:09.520
These... Dammit! Dammit!

00:19:09.520 --> 00:19:11.750
- Why can't I touch them?! Dammit!
- Kyo...

00:19:13.520 --> 00:19:14.620
Dammit...

00:19:15.460 --> 00:19:17.530
Then what are we?

00:19:17.530 --> 00:19:19.590
What does that make us?!

00:19:29.770 --> 00:19:31.370
Those things!

00:19:31.370 --> 00:19:34.340
Altair has made contact with
the enemy! Now engaging!

00:19:34.710 --> 00:19:37.150
Garuda! Hraesvelg! Scramble!

00:19:37.150 --> 00:19:38.770
<i>Stay out of this!</i>

00:19:38.880 --> 00:19:40.580
<i>Everyone, stay out of this!</i>

00:19:40.850 --> 00:19:43.010
<i>Zegapain Altair, starting up.</i>

00:19:43.450 --> 00:19:44.650
These guys are mine!

00:19:59.300 --> 00:20:02.330
It's a lie! It's all a lie!

00:20:08.610 --> 00:20:11.780
<i>I don't believe it! I refuse to accept it!</i>

00:20:11.780 --> 00:20:15.150
<i>We're all fakes? We're all just illusions?!</i>

00:20:15.520 --> 00:20:17.280
<i>Because our bodies were destroyed?!</i>

00:20:17.390 --> 00:20:19.120
<i>Because we can't touch a flower?!</i>

00:20:19.120 --> 00:20:22.580
<i>That's impossible! It's totally impossible!</i>

00:20:23.060 --> 00:20:24.630
I refuse to believe...

00:20:24.630 --> 00:20:26.560
that you things
are more real than me!

00:20:39.740 --> 00:20:43.050
The flowers... They're all dead.

00:20:43.050 --> 00:20:45.540
Yeah. I'm sorry.

00:20:45.820 --> 00:20:50.340
We can't even die like them, can we?

00:20:51.450 --> 00:20:54.890
It's not true... It just can't be true!

00:20:56.890 --> 00:21:01.590
Maybe it's impossible for now,
but some day, we'll be real again.

00:21:02.130 --> 00:21:04.370
The day will come
when we'll be human again!

00:21:04.370 --> 00:21:05.730
Kyo.

00:21:06.000 --> 00:21:08.570
It'll come! I swear it will!

00:21:08.570 --> 00:21:12.440
When we can stand on the ground...
and touch these flowers!

00:22:51.470 --> 00:22:55.410
Someone has transmitted the location
of the Maihama server to the Gards-orm.

00:22:55.410 --> 00:22:58.850
The Anti-Zega Coatlicue
is now coming to destroy it!

00:22:58.850 --> 00:23:01.380
Why isn't Shima fighting it?

00:23:01.380 --> 00:23:04.690
I have a feeling I know who
gave them the information.

00:23:04.690 --> 00:23:08.290
And why do you look like your
duties have gotten the better of you?

00:23:08.290 --> 00:23:12.930
You were the one who decided how
this meal would taste, Shizuno.

00:23:12.930 --> 00:23:15.900
Next time, on Zegapain: "Last Supper."

00:23:15.900 --> 00:23:18.430
My pain, never to be forgotten.
